  "id": "tax.us.2025.rule.sli-worksheet",
  "notes": "Successor to the v4 worksheet. One live path, combined, is active whenever any current Form 1098-E box 1 exists. It reads one combined-standing result per form, beside the four shared answers the worksheet still asks. It does not choose between the older yes/no path and the loan-link path, and it does not refuse because both are present. The arithmetic \u2014 the cap, the phase-out, filing status, scope, and the applicability-marker count \u2014 is the v4 loan-link arithmetic, reading combined standing where that path read statement-line21-standing. The only favorable combined value is none. The second path, inert, names tax.us.2025.sli.inert-path-unwritten. Nothing writes that fact type. The path exists because this rule stays rule-artifact.v13, and that schema requires two paths; the owner kept the inert path rather than a one-path schema. The path never activates. If that fact type becomes current beside a box 1, both paths are active and the selection refuses. If it becomes current alone, the path blocks. The default publishes 0 only for a closed family with no box 1.",
